Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Audit:=20know=20the=20PicoFox=20over=20its=20dr?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ive=20=E2=80=94=20board.json=20carries=20the=20UID;=20listen=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?follows=20the=20banner's=20board?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A PicoFox on fox-bench firmware audited as "unmatched · no deploy on record":
its deploys go over the drive, which has no UID to log, while the console
banner has one, so the audit searched the log for a UID no row carried.

firmware 0.1.4: at boot the fox keeps board.json current on the FOXBENCH
drive — {"board","uid","foxlib"} — rewritten only when it differs. Host
sim stub updated; README lists the file.

page: readDrive() reads board.json into app.info (uid, firmware) so foxlib-c
deploy rows are stamped with the chip UID like REPL deploys; the status line
and a console note show it, and a drive without it (older firmware) says the
deploy is logged without a UID. The demo FOXBENCH drive seeds board.json
with the demo console's UID.

audit.match(): a UID no deploy carries falls back to that board's last deploy
that was itself logged without a UID ("matched by board (that deploy was
logged without a UID)") — never to another identified fox's row — so the rows
already in a fleet log keep matching.

Listen on another board's banner: the console log showed REPL ^C probes and
"no REPL prompt" against the PicoFox — Listen had been started with the XIAO
selected, so a later action talked REPL to the fox-bench console. A banner
naming a catalog board now selects it and puts the matching device (console
or REPL) on the open port.

Tests: audit unit tests for the fallback and the drive-with-board.json path;
smoke checks the stamped deploy row and a drive audit matched by uid.

